WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.430 --> 00:00:02.690
Click Notebook in the sidebar.

2
00:00:02.720 --> 00:00:06.690
The sample workspace already contains an
assembly page, with its notes

3
00:00:06.720 --> 00:00:11.130
and linked sequence records. To keep your
own observations separate, click

4
00:00:11.160 --> 00:00:15.050
the plus button for a new page in SEAL
Sample Notebook.

5
00:00:15.080 --> 00:00:17.240
Give the page a useful title.

6
00:00:17.270 --> 00:00:20.370
Here, type Sequence review practice.

7
00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:24.960
Click in the page body and write two short
observations: which example

8
00:00:24.990 --> 00:00:27.930
you reviewed, and what you checked in
Overview.

9
00:00:27.960 --> 00:00:30.330
Add a new line for the next action.

10
00:00:30.360 --> 00:00:34.190
In this example, the next step is to
compare the translation with

11
00:00:34.220 --> 00:00:38.530
the protein block. The page remains marked
Draft, and the app saves

12
00:00:38.560 --> 00:00:40.730
the text locally as you work.

13
00:00:40.760 --> 00:00:44.460
Click the assembly page in the page list,
then return to Sequence

14
00:00:44.490 --> 00:00:48.378
review practice. Your title and review text
are still present.
